n the road about Misty: she runs WATER-types — a whole gym over a pool; grass and electric do the work YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): You started in Pallet Town, crossed Route 1-2 and Viridian Forest, and beat Brock in Pewter City for the Boulder Badge. Now you\'re pushing on toward the next gym.. Next on my list: catch an pikachu around Viridian Forest (rare) / Power Plant later. It grows into my raichu — that\'s my answer for Misty AND Lorelei down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "Why don\'t you go upstairs and try trading POK.MON with your friends? You could get a lot more variety by trading. The POK.MON you get in trades grow quickly, to"; "That cruise ship S.S. ANNE is in VERMILION CITY. I hear there are lots of TRAINERS on board, too. They invited me to their party, but I can\'t stand fancy do\'s. "; "Wait till I get inside the TELEPORTER. When I do, go to my PC and run the Cell Separation System."; "Hello, are you here alone? If you\'re out at CERULEAN\'s cape.. Well, it should be as a couple.". YOUR PLAN — right now: get abra and ekans to L16-17 fast. Next: Make your way to Cerulean City. Bigger picture: Reach Cerulean City, beat Misty for the Cascade Badge. Your team right now: wartortle (L27), caterpie (L8), rattata (L12), spearow (L13), abra (L13), ekans (L12). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.', 'progress': "1 badge(s) earned (Boulder). Next gym: Misty of Cerulean City. Pokédex: 7 caught. She's one badge in — the adventure's really starting (of 8 badges, then the Elite Four).", 'party': 'wartortle (L27), caterpie (L8), rattata (L12), spearow (L13), abra (L13), ekans (L12)', 'goal': {'short': 'get abra and ekans to L16-17 fas